# The first cells of every documentation notebook

Each notebook `docs/source/NN-Title/index.ipynb` starts with these two cells,
then the demos. They run against real AWS with the test profile, in the CI
resources made by `mise run setup-aws-ci`, so a notebook never needs other
resources or credentials.

## Markdown cell

```markdown
## Setup

This cell only prepares the notebook: it connects to the S3 bucket that the <package_name> CI uses and empties the folder of this chapter, so every run starts from the same state. In your own code you only need the two lines marked below, with your own AWS profile and bucket.
```

## Code cell (example: S3; use the library's own client setup)

```python
import os

import boto3

boto_ses = boto3.Session(profile_name=os.environ["<PACKAGE_NAME>_TEST_AWS_PROFILE"])
s3_client = boto_ses.client("s3")  # <-- in your code
aws_account_id = boto_ses.client("sts").get_caller_identity()["Account"]
bucket = f"{aws_account_id}-{boto_ses.region_name}-<package-name>-test"  # <-- your bucket

# every demo of this chapter writes under this folder; start from empty
prefix_chapter = "projects/<package_name>/docs/NN-Title/"
# ... delete everything under prefix_chapter (with the library itself, if it can) ...
print(f"s3://{bucket}/{prefix_chapter}")
```

Rules:

- The profile name only comes from the environment variable; never write a
  profile name, an account id or a secret in a cell.
- The bucket name contains the account id; `mise run docs-run` replaces it with
  `123456789012` before saving, and fails if the real one is still there.
- Each demo writes under `projects/<package_name>/docs/<notebook>/<demo>/`.
